# veridian-aios.com, dpdp.veridian-aios.com and the legacy app.veridian-aios.com
# (one Pages project, three hostnames, the same files) -- Cloudflare Pages response headers.
# WO-DPDP-012 §2 for the private prefixes, §1 for everything.
#
# How Cloudflare applies this file (its own docs): a request inherits the
# headers of EVERY rule whose pattern matches, in file order, and a header
# name attached twice is comma-joined. So each private rule must first
# DETACH ("! Name") the site-wide Referrer-Policy, in its own rule, before
# a second rule sets the stricter one -- otherwise /app/ would be sent
# "strict-origin-when-cross-origin, no-referrer". src/lib/public-surface.test.ts
# and scripts/check-public-surface.mjs model exactly these merge rules and
# pin the outcome for every private prefix and every public page.
#
# /ai/* is served by a Pages Function (functions/ai/), which sets these same
# headers itself -- _headers only applies to static assets -- but the rule is
# kept here so the one list in public-surface.mjs stays whole.

# Security headers (2026-10-14, audit fixes 15 and 16).
#  * Strict-Transport-Security: browsers must use https for this host for a year. No includeSubDomains and no preload on purpose: other hosts under the
#    domain are not covered by this file, and a preload entry cannot be taken back quickly.
#  * Content-Security-Policy: a real policy. Everything the pages load comes from their own origin (scripts, styles, fonts, images, the service worker,
#    the same-origin /api/ and /ai/ endpoints), plus: the Supabase project (the signed-in app's data calls and signed proof images), and the central payment
#    page that holds the Razorpay window (frame-src only). Styles allow 'unsafe-inline' because the pages carry a few style attributes. No inline script is
#    allowed anywhere, and no page needs one (src/lib/public-surface.test.ts checks this against the built pages).
#    The public pages ALSO allow Cloudflare's Web Analytics script and its report address (disclosed in the Privacy Notice, section 8). The private pages
#    (below: /app/ /act/ /unsubscribe/ /p/ /copy/ /ai/ /api/, the ones a parent or any signed-in person opens) detach that policy and send one WITHOUT them, so
#    the browser refuses Cloudflare's script there (audit fix 16: no tracking script where a child's parent answers). Cloudflare's own automatic injection
#    can also be switched off in the dashboard (ai-os/DPDP_AUDIT_FIX_LIVE_STEPS_2026-10-14.md); this header works even if that is never done.
#  * frame-ancestors / X-Frame-Options: no page may be shown inside another site's frame. Permissions-Policy: no camera, microphone or location.
# _headers applies to static files only; the /ai/* Pages Function (the one that returns pages) sends its own headers (functions/ai/_proxy.ts).
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://pcrjmlpuqsbocqfwoxod.supabase.co; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://pcrjmlpuqsbocqfwoxod.supabase.co https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-src https://itservices-rajat-agarwal.pages.dev; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()

# Caching (speed, 2026-10-01). Only files whose bytes can never change under
# the same URL are cached hard:
#   /assets/*        Vite names every file after its content hash.
#   /original/fonts/* Next.js's hashed font files, frozen with /original/.
#   /fonts/*         the two self-hosted fonts. NOT hashed, so the rule is: never
#                    replace one in place -- ship a new file name and change
#                    src/fonts.css and the preload links to it.
# The brand images keep stable names, so they get a day, not a year.
# The public HTML pages are DELIBERATELY left on Cloudflare Pages' default
# (revalidate on every request, a cheap 304): an HTML page that outlived a
# deploy would point at hashed assets the new deployment no longer holds. And
# there is NO site-wide Cache-Control rule on purpose: Cloudflare comma-joins a
# header attached twice, so a broad rule would turn the private prefixes'
# "no-store" below into "public..., no-store". src/lib/public-surface.test.ts
# and scripts/check-public-surface.mjs pin all of this.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/original/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/og-image.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/logo.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/favicon-48.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/app/*
  ! Referrer-Policy
  ! Content-Security-Policy

/app/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://pcrjmlpuqsbocqfwoxod.supabase.co; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://pcrjmlpuqsbocqfwoxod.supabase.co; frame-src https://itservices-rajat-agarwal.pages.dev; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Cache-Control: no-store

